[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":93},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":-5,"_40":-5,"_41":42,"_43":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":36,"_54":55,"_56":-5,"_57":36,"_58":59},"expiresAt",1795912839000,"id","iumzubpojln46gurdf3hve36s","title","美国空军 Cloud One 云平台据报遭入侵，攻击范围与数据失窃情况未知","originalTitle","US Air Force cloud platform reportedly hacked in latest federal breach","summary","美国空军 Cloud One 云计算平台据报遭黑客入侵，攻击者利用尚未确定的软件漏洞获得访问权限，并可能接触军事行动及后勤敏感信息；平台升级期间发现入侵，应用迁移和软件更新因此中断。","reason","source",{"_66":92},"links",{"_59":91},"publishedAt","2026-11-27T15:09:40.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-27T15:37:20.199Z","timelineAt","category","activity","tags",[67,69,87,71,88,89,90],"score",68,"selected",false,"channel","news","story","x","readingMode","full","author","Lawrence Abrams","body",{"_83":-5,"_59":84,"_85":-5,"_86":36},"outline",[74,75],"relatedStories",[],"topics",[60,61,62,63],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group","hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original",{"_64":72,"_66":73},{"_64":70,"_66":71},{"_64":68,"_66":69},{"_64":65,"_66":67},"slug","attack","name","攻击活动","exploited","在野利用","ai-offense","AI 攻防","supply-chain","供应链安全",{"_11":81,"_77":82,"_79":80},{"_11":76,"_77":78,"_79":80},"sec-2","text","Uncover email threats your existing defenses may miss.","level",2,"sec-1","AI-powered hacking tools fuel cyberattacks","zh","<p><img alt=\"US Air Force logo\" height=\"900\" src=\"/dailyinfo/media/78845badb96a35ae.jpg\" srcset=\"/dailyinfo/media/29f9b232a3060e7f.jpg 720w, /dailyinfo/media/c5bd555e068b1381.jpg 1200w, /dailyinfo/media/78845badb96a35ae.jpg 1600w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1536px) 760px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 524px), (min-width: 640px) 608px, calc(100vw - 32px)\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\"></p><p>Hackers have reportedly breached the US Air Force's Cloud One computing platform, adding to a recent wave of cyberattacks affecting US government agencies, including the FBI, CIA, and Treasury Department.</p><p>According to <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/hackers-breach-us-air-force-flagship-cloud-one-computing-platform-2026-11-27/\">Reuters</a>, the intrusion was discovered within the past month during an upgrade of the cloud platform, disrupting application migrations and software updates.</p><p>Launched in 2017, Cloud One is an enterprise cloud computing platform managed by the US Air Force that allows Department of Defense agencies to host and manage applications supporting military operations, personnel management, logistics, and maintenance.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.wiz.io/lp/claude-code-security-best-practices-cheat-sheet?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&amp;utm_medium=display&amp;utm_campaign=FY27Q3_INB_FORM_Claude-Code-Security-Best-Practices&amp;sfcid=701Vh00000gJQZuIAO&amp;utm_term=FY27Q4-bleepingcomputer-article-970x250-Nov&amp;utm_content=Claude-Code-Best-Practices\"><img src=\"/dailyinfo/media/7a5a3a6292d5f413.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"image\"></a>\n</p><p>According to one source who spoke to Reuters, the hackers exploited an unidentified software vulnerability to gain access to the platform, potentially exposing sensitive military operational and logistics information.</p><p>US Cyber Command has reportedly been called in to assess the impact, with the attackers, scope of the attack, and whether any data was stolen currently unknown.</p><p>The Air Force declined to comment on the security or operational status of the affected systems, telling Reuters that it continuously takes measures to protect its information, systems, and mission capabilities.</p><p>The reported Air Force breach follows other cybersecurity incidents disclosed over the past week targeting US federal agencies.</p><p>On November 21, it was revealed that hackers reportedly <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/fbi-reportedly-hacked-again-this-time-targeting-nationwide-police-database/\">breached the FBI's National Crime Information Center (NCIC)</a>, a nationwide database used by local, state, and federal law enforcement agencies.</p><p>The database contains information on wanted and missing persons, outstanding arrest warrants, stolen vehicles and firearms, and other criminal justice records.</p><p>The intrusion came two months after the <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/shinyhunters-claims-fbi-hack-data-theft-in-peoplesoft-zero-day-breach/\">ShinyHunters extortion group breached FBI systems</a> by exploiting an unpatched Oracle PeopleSoft vulnerability in the agency's recruitment website, FBIJobs.gov.</p><p>Earlier this week, hackers also reportedly <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/hackers-reportedly-breached-cia-intelligence-analysis-system/\">breached an open-source intelligence (OSINT) analysis system</a> at the Central Intelligence Agency (CIA). The incident also affected the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (ODNI) and the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA).</p><p>Hours after the CIA breach was reported, the US Treasury Department's Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN) disclosed that it was investigating unauthorized access to its systems.</p><p>It is unclear whether any of the recently disclosed federal government breaches are connected.</p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">AI-powered hacking tools fuel cyberattacks</h2><p>The CIA breach was reportedly conducted using the ARTEX AI-powered penetration testing platform, which the <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/fbi-warns-artex-ai-hacking-tool-is-powering-global-cyberattacks/\">FBI recently warned</a> was being used to automate cyberattacks worldwide.</p><p>In an advisory, the FBI said multiple threat actors had used ARTEX since at least August 2026 in attacks targeting government, defense, healthcare, financial, and technology organizations.</p><p>ARTEX is an open-source penetration testing framework that uses AI agents to automate various stages of a cyberattack, including discovering and exploiting vulnerabilities, escalating privileges, and stealing data.</p><p>The framework integrates with external AI models from Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT, DeepSeek, Grok, and others, allowing attackers to conduct autonomous attacks against organizations with minimal human intervention.</p><p>According to the FBI, some ARTEX-powered intrusions have progressed from initial targeting to privileged access in less than three hours.</p><p>The platform was used by a Chinese state-aligned threat actor tracked by Microsoft as Storm-0940 in an October <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/hackers-breach-microsoft-365-tenants-via-connectwise-supply-chain-attack/\">attack targeting ConnectWise's Cloud Backup service</a>. Cybersecurity firm Huntress identified at least 162 compromised Microsoft 365 customer tenants during the campaign.</p><p>Other attacks linked to ARTEX include:</p><ul>\n\t<li>Attacks against <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/hacker-used-artex-ai-and-claude-agents-to-target-south-korean-banks/\">South Korean financial institutions</a> that exposed personal information of approximately 67,000 people.</li>\n\t<li>A South Korean hacking campaign <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/former-pentester-used-artex-ai-to-steal-82-million-data-records/\">targeting more than 90 organizations</a>, resulting in the theft of approximately 8.2 million data records and the arrest of seven suspects.</li>\n\t<li>A cyberespionage campaign attributed by CrowdStrike to a Chinese hacking group tracked as Vapor Panda, which <a href=\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/chinese-hackers-use-artex-ai-in-automated-attacks-against-200-orgs/\">targeted more than 200 organizations</a> across 14 countries and compromised at least nine.</li>\n</ul><p>As of early November, researchers had identified more than 1,600 publicly exposed ARTEX management consoles, with the number believed to be much higher.</p><p>It remains unknown whether ARTEX or other AI-powered hacking tools were used in the attacks against the Air Force, FBI, or FinCEN.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/lp/nb/email-scan?utm_source=display_network&amp;utm_medium=paid_display&amp;utm_campaign=2026_NA_Q4_Bleepingcomputer_Inadunit_October2026_scan&amp;utm_id=701Rd00000sqmWCIAY\">\n            <img src=\"/dailyinfo/media/1f6f9d6dc9ced8f5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"article image\">\n        </a>\n    </p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">\n            <a href=\"https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/lp/nb/email-scan?utm_source=display_network&amp;utm_medium=paid_display&amp;utm_campaign=2026_NA_Q4_Bleepingcomputer_Inadunit_October2026_scan&amp;utm_id=701Rd00000sqmWCIAY\">Uncover email threats your existing defenses may miss.</a>\n        </h2><p>Adaptive Security's AI agents analyze email intent, context, and behavior to uncover phishing, business email compromise, and invoice fraud.</p><p>See what's getting through with a 14-day read-only scan of Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace, with no MX changes.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/lp/nb/email-scan?utm_source=display_network&amp;utm_medium=paid_display&amp;utm_campaign=2026_NA_Q4_Bleepingcomputer_Inadunit_October2026_scan&amp;utm_id=701Rd00000sqmWCIAY\">Start your free email security scan.</a>\n    </p>","zhKind","complete","数据泄露","供应链","Microsoft","CrowdStrike","https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/us-air-force-cloud-platform-reportedly-hacked-in-latest-federal-breach/","BleepingComputer",{"_94":95,"_96":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
